e that set them","change":"Hartford's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","rain":"Hartford has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 41\u00b0F was the 14th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 122 since 1905, the coolest since 2019.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 86% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was the 14th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 122 since 1905, the coolest since 2019. The normal high for the date is 52\u00b0F, and the record is 73\u00b0F (1964). The low of <strong>35\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Hartford's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Hartford has set <strong>50 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 81 that chance alone would give, and <strong>114 record highs</strong>, more than the 81 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (42). Hartford's all-time high is 103\u00b0F, on July 22, 2011.","t_chg":"Hartford's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 120 complete years: Hartford's average low shows no clear change: +0.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.05 to +0.10) that includes zero. Hartford's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.30\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +0.36), about +3.6\u00b0F since 1905. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.77\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.45 to +1.09) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.70\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +1.07). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Hartford has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Hartford's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.71 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +1.10), about +8.5 inches since 1905. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 47.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (69.23 in); the driest, 1965 (29.45 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}